Rust has the same root cause: the Rust grammar in the pinned `smacker/go-tree-sitter` snapshot (August 2024) predates raw borrows, `&raw const x` and `&raw mut x`, which have been stable since Rust 1.82. A file that uses one gets `E_PARSE_ERROR`, so Graph cannot list callers of any symbol in that file.

Repro (Entire CLI 0.12.2, Graph v0.6.0) in an empty git repo, with `entire graph health --repo . --json`:

```rust
fn f() {
    let info = 0u32;
    let p = &raw const info;   // E_PARSE_ERROR at 3:14 near "raw const"
    let _ = p;
}
```

`&raw mut` fails the same way; `std::ptr::addr_of!(info)` parses. Once #357 lands, `cmd/grammar-refresh` looks like the way to vendor a current tree-sitter-rust as well.
